  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Humanitarian response &#x2013; Sudanese refugees in eastern Chad</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Oxfam is positioned in Akobo West (Walgak), Akobo East, Uror, Nyirol (Jonglei State), and Minkaman (Lakes State) and maintains Rapid Response teams capable of deploying to emerging hotspots when needed. These locations form the epicentre counties for the current crisis where approximately 80% of displacement is concentrated. The strategic positioning represents years of relationship -building and now provides a critical lifeline for populations that would otherwise be completely abandoned, especially given Government -imposed access restrictions. Oxfam has developed a comprehensive humanitarian response plan to provide immediate life -saving support. Oxfam&apos;s initial response plan covers three months with built -in flexibility to extend based on funding availability and access improvements. The response focuses a) Water, Sanitation, and Hygiene (WASH) interventions to contain cholera through clean water, sanitation, and hygiene promotion; b) Emergency Food Security and Vulnerable Livelihoods (EFSVL) through cash assistance enabling families to buy food and essentials; c) Education in Emergencies providing safe spaces for children; and d) protection programming addressing gender -based violence with gender -sensitive approaches integrated throughout.</narrative>
  </description>
